{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments ["<b>According to your words, so it is.</b> That is to say, he is liable to death, since you have pronounced the verdict; but I do not wish to be harsher upon you beyond the line of justice. <b>With whom it is found.</b> The goblet — he shall be my slave, for such was their law before the giving of the Torah, as it is written above: 'and to take us for slaves, and our donkeys.' But after the Torah was given, he pays double, and if he has nothing, he is sold for his theft."], :book :genesis, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 44, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:08:34.972724441Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}